Yes. I did a broad current sweep across social interfaces, whiteboards, IDEs, scientific/statistical tools, CAD, game-development environments, notebooks, project systems, visualization software, music software, and knowledge-management tools. The important result is that chat is leaving a lot of bandwidth unused.

The best interface for what we’ve been doing would stop treating conversation as only a vertical stream of text and start treating it as a live manipulable model of shared meaning.

The capability harvest

Interface primitive	Where the pattern appears	What I would steal for our interface
